      "summary": "The JWT matcher does not implement the acceptance criterion’s shape-only recognition rule, leaving a reachable path for qualifying tokens to reach logs or traces unredacted.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Diagnostics/RedactionFilter.cs",
          "line": 26,
          "message": "JWT redaction misses tokens that do not start with `e` and does not enforce the required three-segment shape, allowing qualifying JWTs into telemetry.",
          "confidence": 0.99,
          "category": "logic-error",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "Log properties, scopes, and trace attributes pass through ScrubText, which applies Jwt(). Its pattern requires the first segment to start with `ew` or `ey`, and does not enforce the required minimum length on all three segments.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller logs `abcdefgh.ijklmnop.qrstuvwx` under an ordinary property name. It has three base64url segments of at least eight characters, but its first segment does not start with `e`, so Jwt() leaves the token unchanged and it can reach the log provider or trace exporter. The regression test required by the criterion for a header starting with a character other than `e` is also missing. OWASP A09:2025."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
