          "line": 25,
          "message": "JWT redaction misses the required shape and has no regression test for a header starting with a character other than `e`.",
          "confidence": 0.99,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "ScrubText applies Jwt() to log values, scopes, trace tags, and event attributes. Its regex requires the first JWT segment to start with `ew` or `ey`, while the acceptance criterion requires any three base64url segments of at least eight characters.",
            "failureScenario": "If a caller logs or traces `abcdefgh.ijklmnop.qrstuvwx` under an ordinary property name, Jwt() does not match it, so the token reaches the provider or exporter unchanged. The added JWT tests use `e`-prefixed headers and do not catch this required non-`e` case (OWASP A09:2025)."
